From 7654bd3d573be6e33738c5fdd02907cd01e455c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ram Chandra Jangir <rjangir@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2025 12:44:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: Fix MLO capability detection in fragmented netlink
 responses

The GET_WIPHY netlink response is fragmented across multiple messages.
Previously, pWiphy->suppMlo was unconditionally updated on every fragment,
causing the MLO support flag to be reset to false when processing fragments
that don't contain the NL80211_ATTR_MLO_SUPPORT attribute.

This occurred because:
- MLO_SUPPORT attribute was typically in fragment #17 (last fragment)
- New fragments (#18+) were added without MLO_SUPPORT attribute
- The logic `pWiphy->suppMlo = (tb[NL80211_ATTR_MLO_SUPPORT] != NULL)`
  would reset suppMlo to false when processing the new final fragment

This change fixes by only setting suppMlo to true when the attribute is present,
preserving the flag value across fragments that don't contain it.

Change-Id: I0f296341f34765d85d499922aacf170f0dcc9c54
Signed-off-by: Ram Chandra Jangir <rjangir@qti.qualcomm.com>
---

--- a/src/nl80211/wld_nl80211_parser.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_nl80211_parser.c
@@ -1027,8 +1027,10 @@ swl_rc_ne wld_nl80211_parseWiphyInfo(str
     }
     NLA_GET_VAL(pWiphy->nStaMax, nla_get_u32, tb[NL80211_ATTR_MAX_AP_ASSOC_STA]);
     /* check MLO support */
-    pWiphy->suppMlo = (tb[NL80211_ATTR_MLO_SUPPORT] != NULL);
+    if(tb[NL80211_ATTR_MLO_SUPPORT]) {
+        pWiphy->suppMlo = true;
+    }
     s_parseIfTypes(tb, pWiphy);
     s_parseIfCombi(tb, pWiphy);
     s_parseWiphyBands(tb, pWiphy);
